  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Relation between rate constant (k) and absolute temperature (T):</p><p>Arrhenius equation:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mi>RT</mi></mfrac></mfenced></msup></math></p><p>The value of rate constant&nbsp;(k) will increase exponentially with rise in temperature for all type of reactions.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/164a7f3f-5879-4a45-9915-3a765a2d7ae9-e224ef1f-becf-4445-b221-63e0e994f039-image.png\" style=\"width: 225px; height: 224px;\" /></p>",
